  "description": "Single slit with a partially occluded light, the third scene of the diffraction set: the single-slit scene (3 cm light at z = 0.5, two black 30 degree wedge jaws 5 cm apart at z = 0, white wall at z = -1) plus a black rod of 2 cm square cross-section along y, at x in [0, 0.02] and z in [0.24, 0.26]. Seen from the slit's centre the rod hides the right half of the light, and how much it hides changes across the wall. Its four 90 degree edges (UTD n = 3/2) diffract too; they are 4 wavelengths apart, so interactions between edges, which first-order UTD leaves out, are not negligible. Design wavelength 5 mm; scale all lengths with it. The camera stands between the jaws and the wall.",
